    "b-bl-d1": {
      "id": "b-bl-d1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": backfill is a different entry point on the same contract, not a different agent contract. It reuses the envelope, the apply layer, the shared gate, and the stamping rule. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": two write paths would mean two validators drifting apart; the only differences a target-driven pass needs are its context and its population. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the backfill runner and any future bulk pass."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-bl-d2": {
      "id": "b-bl-d2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the population is ranked by material, richest first, and coverage is recorded per subject, so a run can stop and resume at any point and never re-processes a stamped target. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the store has 22,237 targets and most have no material; ranking makes the first batches worth reviewing and stamping makes the run idempotent. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": kg2-prioritize, kg2-backfill, and the --shard striping."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
